  "notes": "ゲット comes from English \"get\" and is used colloquially, especially in casual speech, gaming, and shopping contexts. It conveys a sense of achievement or excitement about obtaining something.\n\nUSAGE:\n- X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ゲット⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to get/obtain X\n- ゲット⟦した→する：00392_suru⟧！: Got it! (exclamation of success)\nPopularized partly through gaming and anime (e.g., ポケモンゲットだぜ！ from Pokémon). Now widely used in everyday casual conversation.\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual. Not appropriate for formal or business contexts. Use ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{入|い}れる→入れる：01098_ireru⟧, ⟦{獲得|かくとく}→獲得：05624_kakutoku⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧, or ⟦{入手|にゅうしゅ}→入手：11636_nyuushu⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ in formal situations.",
